+# smallpt Render Lab
+
+Kevin Beason's smallpt C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly, with a client-side canvas interface. Open the static site's `index.html` through your hosting environment. Rendering uses a dedicated Web Worker; no rendering service or server processing is required.
+
+The page starts a render automatically. Randomize colors creates a fresh palette for the walls and the mirror and glass spheres and starts another render. Individual swatches, sample counts, and resolution can also be changed. Save image exports the current canvas as a PNG.
+
+## Build
+
+Requires Emscripten (`emcc`) on PATH:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This regenerates `public/smallpt.js`, `public/smallpt.wasm`, and the source displayed in the interface. Compiled assets are included, so using the page does not require a local compiler. Serve the project root as static files, preserving the `public/` directory. Workers and WebAssembly require HTTP(S), rather than opening the page through `file://`.
+
+`src/smallpt-original.cpp` preserves the upstream 99-line source. `src/smallpt.cpp` adapts the render loop to a row-based RGBA API and adds color setters, retaining the original camera, sphere intersections, and light transport. `public/preview.png` was rendered by the native build of the same adaptation (640 × 480, 128 spp) and appears while the first live render is initialized.
+
+Original project: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/ — Kevin Beason, 2008. MIT license in `src/LICENSE.smallpt.txt`.
